Well, I don't think there's any *right* way to play any of the classes,
and so I'm specifically trying to avoid saying "you need to do <x, y,
or z>".  Exceptions are, of course, made when I feel appropriate (in
the quoted case, for instance, I really don't think many new players
can survive using the bullwhip as a primary weapon until they get a
better one).  Also, there's no guarantee of finding a mattock,
Grayswandir, of either of the *brands; my current character (lawful
valk) is mapping Gehennom right now, and hasn't seen any of those
weapons.

Regardless, my intention is to help players through the early game;
once you hit solid mid-game, most characters can be played in similar
patterns (ie., knife throwers, spell casters, #twoweaponers), with only
minor variations.  Is there really that much difference between a
late-game valk and a late-game barbarian?

Also, archeologists are a flexible class; saying that they're only good
when wielding a mattock or #twoweaponing is limiting your options, in
my opinion.

